flowchart TD
    A[User opens dashboard] --> B{Choose an action}
    B -- Create a booklet --> B2{Any existing booklets?}
    B2 -- No --> C[Show Create your first booklet]
    B2 -- Yes --> D[Show Create a new booklet]
    C --> E[User opens creation chat]
    D --> E
    B -- Resume incomplete draft --> G[Restore the last incomplete step]
    G --> CONTINUE[Continue at the restored workflow step]

    E --> H[User provides a short storyline<br/>by text or voice]
    H --> I[Autosave draft]
    I --> J[Agent assesses story coherence]
    J --> K{More information needed<br/>and fewer than 8 questions asked?}
    K -- Yes --> L[Agent selects the next relevant<br/>question-card type]
    L --> M[User answers or accepts<br/>a recommendation]
    M --> N[Autosave answer]
    N --> J
    K -- No --> O[Agent presents editable<br/>story overview]

    O --> P[User reviews and optionally edits]
    P --> Q[Accept edits and autosave<br/>without reopening questions]
    Q --> R[Agent selects a suggested cast<br/>from character inventory]
    R --> S[User confirms cast and optionally<br/>edits names or simple traits]
    S --> T[Autosave cast]
    T --> U[Agent retrieves 2 to 5<br/>suitable inventory styles]
    U --> V[User selects one style]
    V --> W[Autosave style]
    W --> X[Agent creates cover + 5-page structure<br/>and selects a representative moment]
    X --> Y[Generate mocked preview panel]
    Y --> Z{User accepts preview?}
    Z -- No, first feedback --> AA[User gives text or voice feedback]
    AA --> AB[Regenerate and show preview once]
    AB --> AC{Confirm final generation?}
    Z -- Yes --> AC
    AC -- No --> AD[Keep autosaved draft]
    AC -- Yes --> AE[Start mocked asynchronous generation]
    AE --> AF[Return to dashboard]
    AF --> AG[Show booklet status: Generating]

    ERR[Recoverable error] --> RETRY[Explain failure, preserve draft,<br/>and offer retry]
    RETRY --> CONTINUE
    L -. failure .-> ERR
    R -. failure .-> ERR
    U -. failure .-> ERR
    Y -. failure .-> ERR
    AE -. failure .-> ERR
